<title>USA: James Jacobson returns as NYSE vice-chairman.</title>
<headline>James Jacobson returns as NYSE vice-chairman.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said on Thursday it elected James Jacobsen vice chairman.</p>
<p>He replaces William Johnston, who became president and chief operating officer of the NYSE on July 1, a statement from the NYSE said.</p>
<p>Jacobsen is a senior managing member of Benjamin Jacobsen and Sons Llc since 1968, the statement said.</p>
<p>Jacobsen was a director of the NYSE from 1987 to 1993 and was vice chairman from 1992 to 1993, the statement said.</p>
